hand over control of its Bashiqa military base in northern Iraq to Baghdad, Ankara and Baghdad said Wednesday, in a move aimed at strengthening Iraqi state authority and easing a long-running source of tension between the neighbours.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Iran will 'never bend at the knee', Pezeshkian tells UN in defiant wartime address</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5a985a3991bdc1d51cb359f9b17795f9f592be0df0272a5766e1c8fa2dc55c05</id><updated>2026-09-24T05:03:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T15:49:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260923-iran-will-never-bend-at-the-knee-pezeshkian-tells-un-defiant-wartime-address--10f22d78db02.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260923-iran-will-never-bend-at-the-knee-pezeshkian-tells-un-defiant-wartime-address" /><summary type="html">Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian gave a defiant wartime address at the UN on Wednesday accusing the US of terrorism in his country and saying Iran would not "bend at the knee". But as Pezeshkian called for diplomacy, Iranian officials downplayed their talks with US counterparts on the sidelines of the gerenal assembly as "not anything new".</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Iran’s Pezeshkian tells UN his country is ‘victim’ of US ‘terrorism’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:01bf8aec8e53034808878769d919ba86f2c15a69ac12103e7a47a40208ae8e5a</id><updated>2026-09-24T05:03:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T14:57:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/iran-s-pezeshkian-tells-un-his-country-is-victim-of-us-terrorism--68195566b037.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/iran-s-pezeshkian-tells-un-his-country-is-victim-of-us-terrorism" /><summary type="html">Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian has hit back at US President Donald Trump’s speech in his address to the UN General Assembly. He opened by showing images of Iranian civilians killed in US strikes, saying they demonstrated the impact of US and Israeli military action against Iran. During his speech, the US delegation walked out of the General Assembly hall. France 24 International Affairs Editor Kethevane Gorjestani has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>REPLAY: Iranian President Pezeshkian adresses UNGA</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9bd4c94da86cf57582bb441ad4399a2bfdee8dfc9e5bdecb33fdd898ba1ff120</id><updated>2026-09-24T05:03:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T14:44:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260923-replay-iranian-president-pezeshkian-adresses-unga-1--ba655932baa6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260923-replay-iranian-president-pezeshkian-adresses-unga-1" /><summary type="html">Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian is speaking before the UN General Assembly Wednesday in his first speech at the world body since the US and Israel launched the conflict with his country. His address comes a day after US President Donald Trump told the UNGA he could "annihilate the Islamic Republic" and "drive them into hell".</summary></entry><entry><title>Golan Heights will 'remain Syrian', President Ahmed al-Sharaa vows at UN</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:159c6d7563bfc9e7de98caac1fa5b399e31c4f57620e7812071bdfe935c5f718</id><updated>2026-09-24T05:03:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T13:31:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260923-golan-heights-will-remain-syrian-president-al-sharaa-vows-to-un--f84fe9f69d85.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260923-golan-heights-will-remain-syrian-president-al-sharaa-vows-to-un" /><summary type="html">Syria's President Ahmed al-Sharaa told the UN Wednesday that the contested Golan Heights region would "remain Syrian" despite ongoing military occupation by Israel. The Syrian leader also used his second turn at the UN rostrum to denounce repeated Israeli strikes on his country.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>UN General Assembly enters second day with key speeches ahead</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:26ee80455f75222307c9a99df797b2b5982e59931dd070bbbb3e1a24f49670d0</id><updated>2026-09-24T05:03:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T13:10:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/un-general-assembly-enters-second-day-with-key-speeches-ahead--5f17c5aa8caa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/un-general-assembly-enters-second-day-with-key-speeches-ahead" /><summary type="html">It’s Day Two of the United Nations General Assembly in New York, with a packed programme including speeches by Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian and Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky. Some of the biggest names in artificial intelligence will also address the UN Security Council. France 24’s Jessica Le Masurier is covering the gathering for us.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israel denounces Macron's UN remarks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1d874c95c90ff12c56089c42a7d2abb8bde86d355da2dff2082ece837ae43dfe</id><updated>2026-09-24T05:03:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T11:56:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/israel-denounces-macron-s-un-remarks--1be41b7349b7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israel-denounces-macron-s-un-remarks" /><summary type="html">Israeli officials have hit back at French President Emmanuel Macron after he criticised Israel’s conduct in the occupied West Bank during his address to the UN General Assembly. But while Macron used strong words against Israel, France allowed Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu’s plane to fly through French airspace on its way to New York, despite an ICC arrest warrant against him. Delano D’Souza reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>US President warns Tehran at UN but says talks ongoing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:24b93c2c37cd9d24a520c29b52b8debaf5e9a0a27603248b4646eef03f855cdb</id><updated>2026-09-24T05:03:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T10:46:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-president-warns-tehran-at-un-but-says-talks-ongoing--e226200bdb56.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-president-warns-tehran-at-un-but-says-talks-ongoing" /><summary type="html">The day began with Donald Trump threatening to annihilate Iran but ended with a three-hour meeting between US and Iranian mediators, which Trump described as “very good.” Trump also held a high-level meeting with Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky, with both sides saying they wanted the war in Ukraine to end before winter. Today, as the UN General Assembly continues, Zelensky and Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian are among those expected to address the assembly, as world leaders seek ways to end the two conflicts dominating international politics. France 24 International Affairs Editor Kethevane Gorjestani shares further insights.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israel blasts ‘grotesque absurdity’ of Macron’s UN remarks on West Bank</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b3f044de4c4990211a249afa99e5b759a334a85ef59851776f074de9118fbecf</id><updated>2026-09-24T05:03:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T08:41:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260923-israel-blasts-grotesque-absurdity-of-macron-s-un-remarks-on-west-bank--342a531dbd98.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260923-israel-blasts-grotesque-absurdity-of-macron-s-un-remarks-on-west-bank" /><summary type="html">The Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's office on Wednesday issued a stinging rebuke to French President Emmanuel Macron's UN speech denouncing settler violence against Palestinians in the West Bank. Macron's remarks that "Hamas has never struck in the West Bank" was a "grotesque absurdity", said the statement.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>US President Trump threatens "annihilation" of Iran despite successful talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7d8116d101c0cff4e3694a387f25e05a4748ef10150b557f3f9950955a428dd2</id><updated>2026-09-24T05:03:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T08:22:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-president-trump-threatens-annihilation-of-iran-despite-successful-talks--ffdddb023d23.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-president-trump-threatens-annihilation-of-iran-despite-successful-talks" /><summary type="html">The day began with Donald Trump threatening to annihilate Iran but ended with a three-hour meeting between US and Iranian mediators, which Trump described as “very good.” Trump also held a high-level meeting with Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky, with both sides saying they wanted the war in Ukraine to end before winter. Today, as the UN General Assembly continues, Zelensky and Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian are among those expected to address the assembly, as world leaders seek ways to end the two conflicts dominating international politics. First, Morgan Ayre reports on the latest developments in the Middle East.</summary></entry><entry><title>AI risks, Iran war dominate agenda at UN</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:be76897262af1f62e9ef4bf2911f7c2fed21f36e98ac581ad2d6eb84bb94b0b8</id><updated>2026-09-24T05:03:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T05:29:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260923-ai-risks-iran-war-to-take-center-stage-at-un--4b4adc4994fd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260923-ai-risks-iran-war-to-take-center-stage-at-un" /><summary type="html">France convenes a UN Security Council meeting Wednesday on artificial intelligence (AI) and international security, which includes briefings by leading industry figures, including the heads of OpenAI and Anthropic. The meeting comes as world leaders jostle over how to address the risks of the new technology. On the second day of the UN General Assembly, the Iran war is also set to dominate the agenda.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Iran: Trump believes in an agreement after US midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ec13504392946b26db035a7bc9c10ecaf63399135097a19ae5ff74f986d99423</id><updated>2026-09-24T05:03:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T16:17:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-iran-trump-believes-in-an-agreement-after-us-midterms--aa11d208ea3e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-iran-trump-believes-in-an-agreement-after-us-midterms" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump told the United Nations General Assembly on Tuesday that he would have to decide whether to “annihilate” Iran if Tehran fails to reach a deal to end the war in the Middle East.
 
He added that he believed an agreement was possible after the US midterm elections in November.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump says envoys Witkoff, Kushner met with mediators on potential Iran deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3cf6e2c65ae1c1df11565498676db19f6a29dfa184a6122ee16467400fa540b5</id><updated>2026-09-24T05:03:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T03:41:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260922-middle-east-live-yemen-fighting-escalates-as-trump-heads-to-un--4465411a8b3f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260922-middle-east-live-yemen-fighting-escalates-as-trump-heads-to-un" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump on Tuesday said ‌special envoys ‌Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner had met ‌with mediators on a possible deal to end the US war against Iran. Trump earlier threatened to "annihilate the Islamic Republic" if Tehran didn’t reach a peace deal with Washington in his UN General Assembly speech. Read about the day’s events as they unfolded on our liveblog.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Saudi Arabia left without US help against Houthis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:153399040d995023ce27968dabf777fca53f263ac7ba4d61e210966ee95428bd</id><updated>2026-09-24T05:03:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T14:57:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/saudi-arabia-left-without-us-help-against-houthis--69e955589d82.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/saudi-arabia-left-without-us-help-against-houthis" /><summary type="html">Saudi Arabia is weighing Washington’s refusal to help fend off Houthi attacks after Riyadh requested US assistance, despite the two countries being longstanding allies and President Donald Trump and his family maintaining close personal ties with Saudi leaders. France 24 International affairs commentator Douglas Herbert shares further details on this alliance.</summary></entry><entry><title>Two tankers hit by 'unknown projectile' or debris in Strait of Hormuz</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9727416e6555d50bd72bd95dfa5a7654fb036f71e57099455d304b895660daba</id><updated>2026-09-24T05:03:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T14:03:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260921-projectile-hits-tanker-as-it-enters-the-strait-of-hormuz--07400cdd3c71.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260921-projectile-hits-tanker-as-it-enters-the-strait-of-hormuz" /><summary type="html">Two tankers were hit in the Strait of Hormuz on Monday by either an "unknown projectile" or debris, a maritime security agency said. United Kingdom Maritime Trade Operations added that at least two crew members were injured in the first incident, and both vessels will continue to their next port of call.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>West Bank: Israeli settler, Palestinian killed in latest violence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:877b9f465dd55ed63bb0d07854b5535f3761a6b29ed22898b4e5fa6c01b50701</id><updated>2026-09-24T05:03:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T12:58:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/west-bank-israeli-settler-palestinian-killed-in-latest-violence--ac92b7366cc1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/west-bank-israeli-settler-palestinian-killed-in-latest-violence" /><summary type="html">Violence flared in the Israeli-occupied West Bank on Sunday, as Israeli forces arrested a suspected Palestinian gunman accused of killing an Israeli man. In a separate incident, Israeli soldiers killed a Palestinian driver who the military said had attempted to run them over. Nicholas Rushworth reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israeli settler and Palestinian driver killed in West Bank shootings</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:09df011bd7cd05edb2321a0bccbf38d5b2521df921554abc28b6581dde9ec1ac</id><updated>2026-09-24T05:03:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T15:30:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260920-israeli-settler-and-palestinian-driver-killed-in-west-bank-shootings--6ec13ca89571.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260920-israeli-settler-and-palestinian-driver-killed-in-west-bank-shootings" /><summary type="html">A suspected Palestinian gunman on Sunday shot dead an Israeli man near a West Bank settlement, according to Israeli officials. The gunman was located at a Ramallah hospital and arrested, police said. Elsewhere in the West Bank, Israeli soldiers killed a Palestinian motorist who the military said was attempting to run them over. The flare up in violence came on the eve of the Jewish holy day of Yom Kippur.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>An Israeli settler and a Palestinian driver killed in West Bank shootings</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:549cf6d2dd407191de6320c9f5275cab1b042df03692e0bed99e9423ead1c6cf</id><updated>2026-09-24T05:03:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T14:34:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/an-israeli-settler-and-a-palestinian-driver-killed-in-west-bank-shootings--7750aafd0f5a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/an-israeli-settler-and-a-palestinian-driver-killed-in-west-bank-shootings" /><summary type="html">An Israeli settler has been fatally shot in the occupied West Bank, while Israel's military said it killed a man who attempted to ram his vehicle into troops elsewhere in the Palestinian territory. The news came as violence in the West Bank is escalating at a very rapid pace. “All Israeli military authorities involved with the West Bank have been warning the Israeli government that the situation is basically out of control”, explains FRANCE 24 correspondent Noga Tarnopolsky.</summary></entry><entry><title>Iran closes French language centre in Tehran for ‘illegal acts’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9a4e3814d30b50a9972622a1b713d5f650ccdb6c1498dd1d9415d014ab36d5e7</id><updated>2026-09-24T05:03:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T13:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260920-iran-closes-french-language-centre-in-tehran-for-illegal-acts--e9366397fe37.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260920-iran-closes-french-language-centre-in-tehran-for-illegal-acts" /><summary type="html">Iranian authorities on Sunday shut down the French Language Centre (CLF) in Tehran, alleging the French embassy-linked institute conducted "illegal acts that violated diplomatic conventions" and "abused its status as a language training facility". France has vowed to take "appropriate measures" in response.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>The week in pictures: Syria protests, Céline Dion on stage and Quito wildfires</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:93c0939360e19a7a8413517b67a0827e2b4867334d3f5a1065ab82dc0abd1118</id><updated>2026-09-24T05:03:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T13:15:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260920-the-week-in-pictures-syria-protests-c_line-dion-on-stage-and-quito-wildfires--7c494f9fc87e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260920-the-week-in-pictures-syria-protests-c%C3%A9line-dion-on-stage-and-quito-wildfires" /><summary type="html">From protests against rising fuel prices in Syria to Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney’s EU charm offensive to Quito’s wildfires and Céline Dion’s return to the stage, FRANCE 24 looks back at the week's most striking pictures.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Houthi attacks and no Western support: What are Saudi Arabia's options ?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:94d5d878dc4899e6b5db3454415b4a44728a29c32e5d75f82eba407e1ca97d84</id><updated>2026-09-24T05:03:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T12:24:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/houthi-attacks-and-no-western-support-what-are-saudi-arabia-s-options--12b32e145452.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/houthi-attacks-and-no-western-support-what-are-saudi-arabia-s-options" /><summary type="html">The US has warned that fighting between Saudi Arabia and Iran-backed Houthis could rapidly escalate. It comes after a missile attack targeted Riyadh for the first time since the Yemen conflict resumed. The Houthis' lightning offensive seized swathes of Yemeni territory in recent weeks and has left hundreds dead. In the face of such attacks and with no support from its American ally, what are Saudi Arabia’s options?</summary></entry><entry><title>'NAZA' documentary about Gaza war sparks political storm in Israel</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:25153b7a0bf0a2a1093f9e97647f0106e0b24dc031ca9e5a43b092c6d467a631</id><updated>2026-09-24T05:03:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T12:22:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/naza-documentary-about-gaza-war-sparks-political-storm-in-israel--e9ca19249009.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/naza-documentary-about-gaza-war-sparks-political-storm-in-israel" /><summary type="html">The Israeli filmmakers behind the documentary NAZA may have received a standing ovation at the Venice film festival, they have been facing violent threats to their lives and citizenship at home in Israel. A month ahead of crucial elections, the film profiles anonymous military sources who speak about the widespread killing of civilians in Gaza. Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said he intends to introduce legislation aimed at revoking the citizenship of people who "defame IDF soldiers". Details by Shirli Sitbon, FRANCE 24 international affairs editor.</summary></entry><entry><title>Why doesn't the US intervene to defend Saudi Arabia against the Houthis?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1c7f384f683c281243d439d94f4d61f9bbe754f27e9064c35241cbfdb1ba87cf</id><updated>2026-09-24T05:03:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T12:20:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/why-doesn-t-the-us-intervene-to-defend-saudi-arabia-against-the-houthis--e9d56b00d69a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/why-doesn-t-the-us-intervene-to-defend-saudi-arabia-against-the-houthis" /><summary type="html">The US cautioned against a rapidly escalating situation in Yemen after Houthi rebels carried out a missile attack on the Saudi capital. In recent weeks, the Iran backed militants have also seized large portions of Yemeni territory following clashes with Saudi-backed government forces. The US is a very close ally to Saudi Arabia. Yet, is visibly unwilling to intervene on its behalf – why? Details and analysis by H. A. Hellyer, senior fellow in geopolitics at the Royal United Institute in Cairo.</summary></entry><entry><title>Yemen's Houthis strike Saudi capital Riyadh for the first time</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8df039f2ad73be615889fecc8fb1d22492de6c2820c250254ff62a80b07c670d</id><updated>2026-09-24T05:03:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T09:38:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/yemen-s-houthis-strike-saudi-capital-riyadh-for-the-first-time--3eef0d6b1feb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/yemen-s-houthis-strike-saudi-capital-riyadh-for-the-first-time" /><summary type="html">Fighting between Iran-backed Houthi rebels and Saudi Arabia continues to intensify. On Saturday morning, a fire broke out near Riyadh's main airport after Houthis said they launched missiles and drones at Saudi Arabia. On the ground in Yemen, Houthi rebels are pushing east in their fight against Saudi-backed government forces. Story by Caroline Baum.</summary></entry><entry><title>Black smoke seen near Riyadh amid air raid alerts in Saudi Arabia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5f481ce1a7f1225c2fa8400fbe5630eafab0e95017d44c8d918b8cb032f788bc</id><updated>2026-09-24T05:03:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T15:16:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/black-smoke-seen-near-riyadh-amid-air-raid-alerts-in-saudi-arabia--6a862c3c701b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/black-smoke-seen-near-riyadh-amid-air-raid-alerts-in-saudi-arabia" /><summary type="html">⁠Flames and plumes of smoke ‌were ⁠seen ‌rising near ⁠Riyadh airport this afternoon with flights cancelled and delayed. This as fighting between Saudi-backed government forces and Iran-backed Houthi rebels has killed 48 people in recent hours. The rebels staged a lightning offensive this month, seizing swathes of territory in Yemen and launching a barrage of missiles and drones toward Saudi Arabia. Details and analysis by FRANCE 24 international affairs editor, Jamie Smith-Maillet.</summary></entry><entry><title>Saudi Arabia says air defences intercepted Houthi ballistic missile targeting Riyadh</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:222f01e388436c18ea306e8ea62c7ef5ff5ee07b5f896044c99fba51c4aa9911</id><updated>2026-09-24T05:03:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T12:53:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260919-smoke-flames-seen-near-riyadh-airport-major-flight-disruptions-reported--d192137a4871.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260919-smoke-flames-seen-near-riyadh-airport-major-flight-disruptions-reported" /><summary type="html">Saudi Arabia on Saturday confirmed that Yemen’s Houthi rebels tried to attack its capital with a ballistic missile, the first targeting of Riyadh since the escalation in fighting with the rebels. The confirmation came hours after the Houthis said they targeted "sensitive sites" in Saudi Arabia.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israel: 'NAZA' documentary sparks political storm</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e151a23074908c6294dfa489adbcb06aaac9205c822fba549d9bd989e1059dde</id><updated>2026-09-24T05:03:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T12:41:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260919-israel-naza-documentary-sparks-political-storm--19a457356dcb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260919-israel-naza-documentary-sparks-political-storm" /><summary type="html">The documentary film 'NAZA', and its co-directors Yuval Abraham and Rachel Szor, are at the centre of a controversy in Israel.The film, which won an award at the Venice Film Festival, features anonymous Israeli sources accusing the military of intentionally killing numerous civilians in Gaza.Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said on Wednesday that he intended to "strip of their citizenship" those who "defame" the Israeli army.</summary></entry><entry><title>US fears wider Middle East escalation after Houthis attack Riyadh</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e48634114a59f42d959aa2604a84ddcab392528c4b83055dd2f03cfe5fb8651e</id><updated>2026-09-24T05:03:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T11:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260919-us-fears-rapid-escalation-in-mideast-after-houthis-attack-riyadh--2e2fa664288a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260919-us-fears-rapid-escalation-in-mideast-after-houthis-attack-riyadh" /><summary type="html">The United States warned Saturday that fighting between Saudi Arabia and Iran-backed Houthi forces could “escalate rapidly” after a missile attack targeted Riyadh for the first time since the Yemen conflict resumed. The attack prompted US President Donald Trump to cut short a weekend at a secluded presidential complex in rural Maryland and return to the White House.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>More than 112,000 displaced in Yemen as Houthis seize more ground</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e2ccdb0f2f0a9c132ae86355a6316ccbbcc1a02ab3d2ec0eb911d5728898ed71</id><updated>2026-09-24T05:03:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T08:57:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/more-than-112-000-displaced-in-yemen-as-houthis-seize-more-ground--fdb60ca50a35.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/more-than-112-000-displaced-in-yemen-as-houthis-seize-more-ground" /><summary type="html">Pro-Houthi demonstrations erupted in Yemen after Saudi Arabia accused the military group of targeting the Muslim holy site of Mecca. Story by Elitsa Gadeva.</summary></entry></feed>
